BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:835a2dbc-4838-4236-b356-bd2a26396219@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T010000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T023000
SUMMARY:Murge
LOCATION:Nectar Stage
DESCRIPTION:A sonic alchemist\, murge weaves the eclectic and the electric 
 to create dancefloor-centric beats that fill the space and lift the crowd.
  unorthodox sounds intertwine to create an expansive aural journey filled 
 with fresh\, earthy bass and neoteric instrumentals.  signed to emancipat
 or’s label loci records in 2020\, murge has had a rapid rise\, winning a
 ccolades from peers and listeners alike and landing features on the bigges
 t dsp editorial playlists. collaborations with emancipator\, parra for cuv
 a\, tor and frameworks followed\, along with support from heavyweights suc
 h as bbc radio 1\, bbc radio 6 and sirius xm.   no stranger to packed dan
 ce floors or epic stages\, murge has entranced crowds at some of north ame
 rica’s most well respected electronic festivals\, including bc’s own b
 ass coast and shambhala\, and has toured extensively throughout the united
  states. 2024 saw the release of his second album 'Gold & Bliss'\, a subli
 me collection of atmospheric new tracks designed to excite and elevate.\n\
 nWebsite: https://djmurge.com\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/murge_
 music/?hl=en\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/3ykuLH14n05EsgIRDZE
 R5W\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/murge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ec5b76ad-6bcd-4baa-9a83-e54a41aca46e@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T023000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T040000
SUMMARY:The Silk Road
LOCATION:Nectar Stage
DESCRIPTION:Explore the world with Yelda and Biplov – an Afghan and Nepal
 ese DJ duo sharing global beats on the dance floor. Together they ignite a
  vision of global connection inspired by the true-life historic Silk Road.
  Their musical diversity of light and dark energy combines forces and crea
 tes the magic of The Silk Road - a journey that showcases instruments and 
 languages from across the world in an effort to spark cultural curiosity a
 nd inclusivity.\n\nTSR has been thrilled to play support for incredible Ar
 tists such as DJ Habibeats\, Beats Antique\, Yung Singh\, Handsome Tiger\,
  Attya\, Moontricks\, Morillo\, Papadosio\, Random Rab\, Desert Dwellers\,
  and Etran de L’Aïr. Notable festivals include Shambhala\, Bass Coast\,
  Future Forest\, Global Heat and APOG.\n\nTheir movement has already taken
  Seattle by storm\, embodied in the creation of CARAVAN – an open format
 \, monthly world music event showcasing both novice and veteran Artists. I
 t is now celebrating over three years of events at Kremwerk Complex and su
 ccessful showcases at APOG Festival\, Panacea and Kremfest.\n\nNow they’
 re gearing up for the next phase of their mission - developing and produci
 ng new tracks to share with the world. They debuted with their original 
 “Rangeela” on Midnight Munchies & officially released their first EP 
 “Ey Sune” in February 2026. Whether at a music festival\, local venues
  or on the air\, TSR seeks to bring people together by celebrating what ma
 kes them culturally unique and inviting them to join the Shawlgang.\n\nWeb
 site: http://www.silkroaddjs.com\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/sil
 kroaddjs/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@silkroaddjs\n\nProfile: https
 ://thenectarfestival.com/products/the-silk-road
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:da4d8a95-5858-485b-b391-b1bd4a2adf26@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T040000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T050000
SUMMARY:Atebaki
LOCATION:Nectar Stage
DESCRIPTION:[downtempo // leftfield // freeform]\n\natebaki brings to the s
 tage his own creative universe\, weaving sounds inspired by flow states an
 d melodies found in dreams.\n\nWith an aim to create an immersive experien
 ce for the listener\, each track unfolds like an origami of emotional stat
 es\, blooming into atebaki’s unique fusion of deep low-end\, futuristic 
 synths and soulful melodies.\n\natebaki’s soundscape is a nectar for the
  senses\, capturing the dance floor inside a bubble\, ready to make bodies
  flow and spirits wander.\n\nThe artistic ethos at the core of atebaki is 
 to make bodies flow and spirits wander. As an artist\, he is obsessed with
  the feelings that arise from the passage of time\, the cycles of death an
 d rebirth and the sorrow of being finite\; in his music\, this translates 
 into a deep journey blending melancholy\, serenity\, romance\, solace and 
 abysmal levity. His sets evolve slowly\; through them he serenades his lis
 teners into the spirit world and keeps them simmering in the infinite feel
 s.\n\n[bio]\n\nVancouver-based producer atebaki was born in Argentina and 
 raised in Montreal. He started out his producer journey from a multidiscip
 linary background\; writing poetry\, playing multiple instruments and prac
 ticing different circus disciplines. His creative universe encompasses mul
 tiple art forms that are all dancing around the same ethos: to make bodies
  flow and spirits wander.\n\nIn order to avoid trapping the audience in a 
 singular emotion\, atebaki carefully crafts each set to be constantly evol
 ving\, exploring a plethora of moods and keeping the flow steady.\n\nWith 
 releases on Gravitas Recordings\, Subciety Presents\, Cimmerian Records an
 d UnderGround Sound\, atebaki has been pushing the boundaries of the downt
 empo side of bass music. His search for a deeper connection with his commu
 nity led him to organize inner space: a downtempo night focused on deep ba
 ss\, immersive art installations and live performances. The motto? come to
  dance\, come to chill\, come to unwind.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud
 .com/atebaki\nInstagram: http://www.instagram.com/atebaki\nBandcamp: http:
 //www.atebaki.bandcamp.com\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/produ
 cts/atebaki
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
